tools.description:
Append new content blocks to a Notion page or block.

**When to call**: The user wants to add text, headings, to-do items,
bullet lists, or any other block-level content at the *end* of an
existing page or inside an existing toggle/column block.

Args:
    block_id: (required) The parent page or block ID to append into.
    children: (required) A list of Notion block objects to append.

              Example — add a paragraph and a to-do:
              ```json
              [
                {
                  "object": "block",
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "paragraph": {
                    "rich_text": [{"type": "text", "text": {"content": "Hello!"}}]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "object": "block",
                  "type": "to_do",
                  "to_do": {
                    "rich_text": [{"type": "text", "text": {"content": "Buy milk"}}],
                    "checked": false
                  }
                }
              ]
              ```

Returns:
    **Success** — confirmation + list of created block IDs.

    **Failure** — error reason + guidance.

Example:
    append_notion_blocks(
        block_id="page-id-here",
        children=[{"object":"block","type":"paragraph","paragraph":{
            "rich_text":[{"type":"text","text":{"content":"New paragraph"}}]
        }}]
    )

Run a funnel analysis report to visualize user conversion paths.

**When to call:**
When the user wants to analyze step-by-step conversion funnels,
e.g. "homepage → product page → add to cart → checkout → purchase".

**Parameters:**
- property_id: GA4 property ID.
- funnel_json: JSON string with the full funnel report request body
  including dateRanges and funnel definition with steps.

**Example funnel_json:**
{
  "dateRanges": [{"startDate": "30daysAgo", "endDate": "today"}],
  "funnel": {
    "steps": [
      {"name": "First visit", "filterExpression": {
        "eventFilter": {"eventName": "first_visit"}}},
      {"name": "View item", "filterExpression": {
        "eventFilter": {"eventName": "view_item"}}},
      {"name": "Purchase", "filterExpression": {
        "eventFilter": {"eventName": "purchase"}}}
    ]
  }
}

**Returns:** JSON with `funnelTable` containing step-by-step
user counts and drop-off rates.
